<Base title="About StatusGrid" description="StatusGrid is a practical bulk HTTP status checker and learning resource for technical SEO work."><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">About StatusGrid</span><h1>Make every URL easier to understand.</h1><p>StatusGrid brings a useful status report and plain-language guidance together in one place.</p></div></section><section class="content-section"><div class="container prose"><h2>Why it exists</h2><p>Checking a URL should answer more than “did it return 200?” A redirect may finish on the wrong page. A success response may carry a noindex directive. A broken URL may be one of many in a migration list. StatusGrid groups these clues so you can find the next action faster.</p><h2>What we value</h2><p>Clear reports, inspectable paths, and practical explanations. The tool reports observable HTTP and HTML signals and makes its limits visible. The guides cite primary documentation where search behavior matters.</p><h2>Who it helps</h2><p>Site owners, developers, content teams, and technical SEO practitioners can use it for migration checks, broken-link cleanup, and routine spot audits. It is free to use without creating an account.</p><p><a href="/#checker">Try the bulk checker</a> or read the <a href="/blog/">field guides</a>.</p></div></section></Base>
